From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:11:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: roll back a BSS when AP setup fails
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add() links a new AP BSS into the driver's BSS
list and publishes its context before nl80211_setup_ap(). If management
subscription or monitor setup fails, it returns without releasing that
BSS. The caller clears interface_added, and an MLD context has no valid
links yet, so neither interface nor link cleanup releases it.

The leaked BSS keeps the driver shared and can become its first BSS when
the primary is removed. Its callback context then points at the failed
hostapd_data after the ADD error unwind frees it.

Unlink this secondary BSS on AP setup failure, release its callback
handles, undo bridge changes, and delete the netdev only if this call
created it. Clear the published output after freeing the BSS. A reused
netdev may be held by another live BSS, causing REGISTER_FRAME to fail
with -EALREADY. Keep that netdev up and preserve its ifindex routing;
this BSS has not reached add_ifidx() and has no links to remove.

The primary BSS and successful setup path remain intact. This does not
change the handling of failures before publication or later link-add
failures.

Fixes: 3dd1d8906df9 ("nl80211: Subscribe management frames for WPA_IF_AP_BSS types")
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
index 612e8aaf243b..7e965c878c17 100644
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -9045,8 +9045,28 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_if_add(void *priv, enum wpa_driver_if_type type,
 		nl80211_init_bss(new_bss);
 
 		/* Subscribe management frames for this WPA_IF_AP_BSS */
-		if (nl80211_setup_ap(new_bss))
+		if (nl80211_setup_ap(new_bss)) {
+			/* No link or ifidx was added. A reused netdev may still
+			 * belong to another live BSS; leave it up and registered. */
+			drv->first_bss->next = new_bss->next;
+			nl80211_destroy_bss(new_bss);
+			if (new_bss->added_if_into_bridge &&
+			    linux_br_del_if(drv->global->ioctl_sock,
+					    new_bss->brname, ifname) < 0)
+				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "nl80211: Failed to remove interface %s from bridge %s: %s",
+					   ifname, new_bss->brname, strerror(errno));
+			if (new_bss->added_bridge &&
+			    linux_br_del(drv->global->ioctl_sock,
+					 new_bss->brname) < 0)
+				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "nl80211: Failed to remove bridge %s: %s",
+					   new_bss->brname, strerror(errno));
+			if (added)
+				nl80211_remove_iface(drv, ifidx);
+			os_free(new_bss);
+			if (drv_priv)
+				*drv_priv = NULL;
 			return -1;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (drv->global)
-- 
